commonMistakes:
  - title: "Capitalizing Minor Prepositions in Title Case"
    description: "In Chicago and AP style, minor prepositions, articles, and conjunctions under four letters (e.g., 'in', 'on', 'the', 'and', 'for') remain lowercase unless starting a sentence."
  - title: "Breaking Unicode & Accented Characters"
    description: "Naive case conversion using standard ASCII regex fails on accented letters like 'é' or non-Latin alphabets; Unicode property escapes (\\p{L}) must be used."
  - title: "Losing Delimiters When Converting Code"
    description: "Converting camelCase or snake_case code into sentence case strips programming delimiters. Keep backups or use the Undo button."
  - title: "Title Case on All-Caps Input"
    description: "If all-caps text is fed into a title case engine without initial lower-casing, minor prepositions remain capitalized. Our algorithm normalizes tokens first."
